SEP-11: cross-thread reduction in bgraphBipartGg() compares signed imbalance on communication-load ties.
sep11.c: complete graph K_n, unit edge loads, vertex loads 1+((v*7919)%50), strategy r{sep=h{pass=64}},
SCOTCH_graphPart into 2 parts, prints cut and |load0-load1|. On K_n all bipartitions with the same part sizes
have the same cut, so threads tie on communication load and the imbalance tie-break decides.
Build: gcc -O0 -g -fsanitize=address,undefined -I<include> sep11.c -o sep11 -L<lib> -lscotch -lscotcherr -lz -lm -lpthread
Run:   for s in $(seq 1 40); do SCOTCH_PTHREAD_NUMBER=8 LD_LIBRARY_PATH=<lib> ./sep11 <n> $s; done

